          "id": "p7",
          "text": "G Given the pace of change, bosses need more than ever to be able to communicate persuasively through any channels, which their staff and the outside world. They must also listen: the most valuable communications will frequently be bottom-up, and the people nearest to customer are best placed to explain what they see and hear. Managers must listen to them."
