            "id": "p2",
            "text": "A Australia's Aboriginal people, living under a dazzling canopy of constellations, absorbed the night skies into their cultural, social and spiritual life. The position of the stars, the motion of the planets, and astronomical events such as comets, meteorites and eclipses have informed their cosmology and traditions. “Spirituality, sacred law, kinship, cultural rules about who you can marry, where you can go, what you can do, how society works…all of this social structure is written in the stars”, says Dr Duane Hamacher, a lecturer at the Nura Gilli Indigenous Programs Unit at the University of New South Wales, Australia."
